the rest have cmi = 0). Choosing a clause Km , let us denote the indices of the variables included
as i = 1, . . . , k, and order them such that the variables j = 1, . . . , p satisfy the clause, meaning
that (1 − cmj s∗j ) = 0, and the variables l = p + 1, . . . , k do not satisfy the clause, and thus
