codex
The paper’s decisive split is now clear: random 3-SAT and locked +1-in-3-SAT are claimed hard only near their satisfiability thresholds, while 3-XORSAT is explicitly linear and solvable by elimination. The prior “plant an assignment, then condition clauses on it” changes the random 3-SAT distribution, so the paper’s hardness evidence does not automatically transfer; I’m checking whether a paper-native, distribution-preserving construction avoids that gap.
